# ALERT 1: FilesystemSpaceCritical - fill the filesystem
############################################################

    usage before: 8%

    Filling in steps, checking after each. A single calculated allocation
    undershot on the first attempt - XFS reserves blocks, so 'available'
    is not the same as 'what can still be written' - and it reached only
    70%. The alert correctly did not fire, which is why this loop exists.

